# The paranoid allowlist of a plain segment (docs/paranoid_mode.md). pf apply
# copies this file to /etc/pi-fortress/allow.<segment>.domains, for example
# allow.desk.domains, for each segment in segments.d that has no such file.
# It never writes over a file that exists: after that, it is operator state.
# With PARANOID=on in the segment file, it holds all names that the segment
# may resolve. With PARANOID=off, nothing reads it.
#
# One name per line. A name allows itself and all its subdomains, the same
# as allow.domains. Thus anthropic.com already covers api.anthropic.com
# and *.anthropic.com. A "*.name" line is the same as "name": write
# "name". This file only:
# the allow.domains and core.hosts of the agent do not apply to a segment.
#
# The seed lets Claude Code work on the desk. Apply refuses
# PARANOID=on while the file has no usable name.
anthropic.com
claude.ai
claude.com
